Description: Drop stale watdefs.h references from the makefile
 watdefs.h was intentionally removed from this source tree in 2018,
 in favour of the build-dependency on libpluto-jpl-eph-dev, but five
 build targets (mpc2sof, mpc_code, parallax, parallax.cgi, ps_1996)
 still list it as a literal make prerequisite, and 'install'/
 'uninstall' still try to copy/remove a local copy of it.
 .
 Listing a header as a prerequisite is unrelated to whether the
 compiler can find it via -I: make requires every prerequisite to
 either exist as a file or have a rule to build one, and since no
 such file or rule exists for watdefs.h, make fails outright before
 the compiler is ever invoked:
 .
   make[1]: *** No rule to make target 'watdefs.h', needed by
   'mpc2sof'.  Stop.
 .
 This was never noticed before because these five targets are only
 reachable once every other Debian-specific build issue upstream of
 them (the missing INTENTIONALLY_UNUSED_PARAMETER macro, -Wdate-time,
 the integrat.o include path) has already been fixed.
 .
 Drop watdefs.h from the five prerequisite lists (compilation is
 unaffected either way, since it already finds the header via -I),
 and drop the install/uninstall steps for it, since this package no
 longer owns that file.
Author: Fukui Daichi <a.dog.will.talk@akane.waseda.jp>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-09-07
